The Estonian Supreme Court on Friday partially rehabilitated a man convicted by the Supreme Court of the Estonian SSR in 1979 for attempting to flee the Soviet Union by boat and for stealing weapons, boats and boat engines.
In October 1979, the Supreme Court of the Estonian SSR found Imre Arakas guilty of several anti-state offenses, thefts, illegal possession of weapons and armed attacks. He was sentenced to 15 years in prison with confiscation of all property. The sentence required him to spend the first three years in prison and the remaining 12 years in a high-security correctional labor camp.
Among other charges, he was accused of attempting to leave the Soviet Union without permission, though the attempt failed when the boat's engine malfunctioned and wind and waves carried it back to shore.
